{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3315","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3315","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3315\",\"parent_revision\":\"b83bb72c2cba7c06b0fa90957974a503150a37856c7e12d58adf3937e9f42572\",\"root_revision\":\"b83bb72c2cba7c06b0fa90957974a503150a37856c7e12d58adf3937e9f42572\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-29\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nThe need this serves: avoid rejecting a legitimate new backlog item as a false duplicate when the cached \\\"duplicate\\\" was actually closed or changed on the remote provider since the last sync.\\n\\n**Current design (deliberate, ADR-003 from #3169's architect spec)**: `_classify_duplicate_check` in `backlog_core/operations.py` refreshes the local cache from GitHub only when the local check finds *no* match \u2014 \\\"refresh-on-empty-result only (not every call)\u2014pays network cost exactly when about to declare safe to proceed.\\\" When a local match IS found, `DUPLICATE_FOUND` is returned immediately, with no refresh.\\n\\n**Gap this accepts**: if the cached item that appears to match was actually closed, resolved, or edited on GitHub after the last sync (and the local cache hasn't caught up), the duplicate check rejects the new item based on stale data \u2014 the opposite failure mode from the one #3169 originally fixed (which was \\\"stale cache reports no duplicate when one exists\\\"). This is the same underlying risk, just on the accept/reject boundary rather than the found/not-found boundary.\\n\\n**Trade-off to weigh in grooming**: refreshing on every match (in addition to every non-match) would double the network/refresh cost of every `add_item` call under a `SyncProvider` backend. Options worth considering: refresh only when about to raise `DuplicateItemError` (i.e., right before the hard rejection, not on every match check), a time-based staleness threshold before treating a local match as authoritative, or leaving the current trade-off as-is and documenting it as an accepted limitation.\\n\\n**Source**: Raised during PR #3274 review (automated) against commit f7d49d9cfb, and confirmed as a genuine (if narrow) gap in the shipped design rather than an implementation bug \u2014 not fixed in that PR because it changes documented architectural intent (ADR-003) rather than correcting a defect.\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: PR #3274 review follow-up on #3169 (content-based duplicate detection)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"ddad7e416b44b6f8bd2d4213552ae93044e126a06ba3ed487505af8529564016\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABRZ5Ldw\"}"}